# Build context exclusions. CLAUDE.md § 5: `.env` is excluded from the image build context.
#
# THE FIRST BLOCK IS THE LOAD-BEARING ONE. Everything below it is about image size; this one is
# about a credential ending up in a layer. A file copied into a layer is in that layer forever —
# deleting it in a later instruction does not remove it from the image, and `docker history` on a
# built image is enough to read it back. `.env` is gitignored, which keeps it out of the repo and
# does nothing whatsoever about the build context: `docker build .` sends the working directory,
# not the git index.
#
# `COPY . .` appears nowhere in either Dockerfile — both copy named paths — so this file is the
# second of two independent reasons the secret is not in the image, not the only one.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets/

# Terraform state carries secrets in plaintext (CONTEXT.md records this about the local state file
# sitting in the working tree). It has no business in a build context at all.
infra/terraform/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfvars

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything below is size and reproducibility, not secrecy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# A host-built node_modules is the wrong architecture and the wrong Node version — Phase 9 found
# the instance on Node 18 while the toolchain needs 22 (CONTEXT.md). Dockerfile.frontend runs
# `npm ci` inside the pinned Node image; a host tree copied over it would silently win.
node_modules/
frontend/node_modules/

# A host-built bundle is exactly what decision 6 forbids serving. Excluded so it cannot be copied
# into the frontend image by accident and shadow the one the image builds.
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/

.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage*
htmlcov/

# Documentation and verification apparatus. `verify/` is deliberately excluded: CLAUDE.md § 13
# keeps verification out of `app/`, and shipping it inside the running image would put it back.
CLAUDE.md
CONTEXT.md
docs/
tests/
verify/
scripts/
infra/
docker-compose.override.yml

*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.log
.DS_Store
